data part_standing_note: String = "THE OBSERVING LAYER FOR ALTRA BOARD ROLES. ALTRA-PARTS-0 selected parts and land patterns in extdeps; this module consumes those rows and records coverage observations this repository made, which DESIGN section 3 says must not be authored inside the upstream modules. THE PART/GEOMETRY LADDER IS FOUR RUNGS, not a filled Bool: established MountablePart geometry; part selected with MountingPatternStanding still outstanding; type named but no vendor, part or geometry (ILM4926, cited from extdeps.ocp.mt_jade); and nothing known, split into SelectionNeverAttempted versus AccessRefused. Collapsing any two rungs reports less than the repository knows. FOUR ROLES THAT WERE UNFILLED NOW HAVE NAMED CATALOG ROWS whose geometry is outstanding, so they sit on the same rung as the TE DIMM: the access-refusal is why the pattern is outstanding, not why nothing is known. JUSTIFICATION IS A FIFTH AXIS beside those rungs: it is a relation between a part and this board, so it is authored here rather than in extdeps, and a second board consuming the same part does not inherit it. Three of those catalog rows are named by the parent's report of Mt. Jade and still sit at JustificationOutstanding until a BOM is read; the Samtec header is a session candidate and Mt. Jade names no part number for it. SELECTED-PART DOCUMENTS ARE CITED BY DECLARATION, not by a second copy of the locator the catalog row already carries. Uncited locators remain only for superseded alternatives that have no catalog home. NO CONTACT COUNT IS RECORDED for the Amphenol M.2 row: a drawing has not been read, and a 75-versus-67 disagreement without a drawing is not a fact."

